# Data licences

This repository publishes two kinds of data under two different licences.

## Blocklists: CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain dedication)

Everything under `blocklists/` is released into the public domain under CC0 1.0. Use it in any
resolver, any product, any list, with or without credit.

Full text: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

The intent is maximum uptake. If HaGeZi, Perflyst, oisd, Pi-hole, AdGuard, NextDNS or anyone else
wants to absorb these entries into their own lists, they should not have to ask or attribute.

## Report corpus: ODbL 1.0 plus DBCL 1.0

The crowdsourced report corpus (`data/reports/`) and its published derivatives, including the NDJSON
and Parquet mirrors, are made available under the Open Database Licence 1.0. Rights in the individual
contents of the database are licensed under the Database Contents Licence 1.0.

ODbL 1.0: https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/
DBCL 1.0: https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/dbcl/1-0/

You are free to share, create works from, and adapt the database, provided you attribute, keep any
adapted database open under the same terms, and do not use technical measures to restrict others.

This follows the licence stack used by Exodus Privacy for its tracker database. The reciprocity
matters here in a way it does not for the blocklists: the corpus exists because volunteers contributed
observations about their own homes, and derivatives of it should stay open to the people who built it.

## Curated source data

The files under `data/endpoints/`, `data/hardcoded/`, `data/packages/` and `data/devices.yml` are
curated documentation rather than a crowdsourced database, and are covered by LICENSE-CONTENT
(CC BY 4.0). The generated blocklists derived from them are CC0 as above.
